# strings4 — SET ... GET: swap and see what was there
#
# Learn: SET key value GET writes the new value and replies with the old
# one, in a single atomic command (it replaces the deprecated GETSET).
# A separate GET and SET leaves a gap where another client can write.
#
# Task: deploy a new config version by setting config:active to "v2",
# and print the version that was active before, using ONE command. The
# check compares your output with the previous value.
#

GET config:active
SET config:active v2
